<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-COLLATED AFRICAN NATIONS CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-COLLATED AFRICAN NATIONS CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of African</p>
<p>Nations Cup qualifying matches played on the weekend:</p>
<p>Group One:</p>
<p>In Luanda:</p>
<p>Angola 1 Ghana 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Akwa (23rd minute)</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>Standings (under matches played, won, drew, lost, goals for,</p>
<p>goals against, points):</p>
<p>    Zimbabwe  2  1  1  0  1  0  4</p>
<p>    Ghana     3  1  1  1  2  2  4</p>
<p>    Angola    3  1  0  2  2  3  3</p>
<p>Next match:</p>
<p>Ghana v Zimbabwe, Kumasi, July 12</p>
<p>Group Two:</p>
<p>In Bamako:</p>
<p>Mali 3 Benin 1 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Mali - Bassala Toure (12th), Yaga Dissa (68th), Sadiq Traore</p>
<p>(85th min penalty)</p>
<p>Benin - Keita (40th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>In Bouake:</p>
<p>Ivory Coast 2 Algeria 1 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ivory Coast - Joel Tiehi (44th), Michel Bassole (87th)</p>
<p>Algeria - Kamel Kaci Said (17th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Mali	  4  3  0  1  7  4  9</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast 4  3  0  1  6  6  9</p>
<p>    Algeria     4  1  1  2  6  5  4</p>
<p>    Benin	 4  0  1  3  3  7  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Algeria v Mali, Algiers, July 11</p>
<p>Benin v Ivory Coast, Cotonou, July 13</p>
<p>Group Three:</p>
<p>In Casablanca:</p>
<p>Morocco 1 Egypt 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Saleheddine Bassir (71st)</p>
<p>Attendance: 80,000</p>
<p>In Dakar:</p>
<p>Senegal 3 Ethiopia 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Souleymane Sane (38th, 53rd), Oumar Traore (68th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 28,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Morocco   4  2  2  0  6  1  8</p>
<p>    Senegal   4  2  2  0  5  1  8</p>
<p>    Egypt     4  0  3  1  2  3  3</p>
<p>    Ethiopia  4  0  1  3  2  11 1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Egypt v Senegal, Cairo, July 11</p>
<p>Ethiopia v Morocco, Addis Ababa, July 12</p>
<p>Group Four:</p>
<p>Sierra Leone v Tunisia postponed</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Guinea	  2  2  0  0  2  0  6</p>
<p>    Tunisia	 2  1  0  1  2  1  3</p>
<p>    Sierra Leone  2  0  0  2  0  3  0</p>
<p>Next match:</p>
<p>Tunisia v Guinea, Tunis, July 12</p>
<p>Group Five:</p>
<p>In Nairobi:</p>
<p>Kenya 0 Namibia 1 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorer: Gervatius Uri Khob (35th min)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>In Yaounde:</p>
<p>Cameroon 2 Gabon 2 (halftime 2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Cameroon - Bernard Tchoutang (12th), Cyrille Mangan (33th)</p>
<p>Gabon - Pierre Aubame (38th penalty), Aurelin Bekogo (87th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 60,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Namibia    4  2  1  1  3  5  7</p>
<p>    Cameroon   4  1  3  0  6  2  6</p>
<p>    Kenya	4  1  1  2  1  2  4</p>
<p>    Gabon	4  0  3  1  3  4  3</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Namibia v Cameroon, Windhoek, July 12</p>
<p>Gabon v Kenya, Libreville, July 13</p>
<p>Group Six:</p>
<p>In Arusha:</p>
<p>Tanzania 1 Togo 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Idelfonce Amlima (31st min)</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>In Monrovia:</p>
<p>Liberia 2 Democratic Republic of Congo (formerly Zaire) 1</p>
<p>(half-time 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Liberia - Kelvin Sebwe (20th), George Weah (66th)</p>
<p>DR Congo - Nsiala Nzalambila (81st)</p>
<p>Attendance: 45,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Togo     4  2  1  1  5  4  7</p>
<p>    DR Congo 4  1  2  1  4  4  5</p>
<p>    Liberia  4  1  2  1  4  4  5</p>
<p>    Tanzania 4  1  1  2  4  5  4</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>DR Congo v Tanzania, Kinshasa, July 13</p>
<p>Togo v Liberia, Lome, July 13</p>
<p>Group Seven</p>
<p>In Lilongwe:</p>
<p>Malawi 3 Mauritius 2 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Malawi - John Maduka (19th min, 81st), Hendrix Banda (76th)</p>
<p>Mauritius - Eric Philogene (87th) James Pierre-Louis (89th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>In Maputo:</p>
<p>Mozambique 2 Zambia 2 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Mozambique - Tico-Tico (11th), Chiquinho Conde (62th min</p>
<p>penalty)</p>
<p>Zambia - Frazier Kamwandi (15th), Masauso Tembo (57th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Malawi     4  3  0  1  7  5  9</p>
<p>    Zambia     4  2  2  0  5  2  8</p>
<p>    Mozambique 4  1  1  2  5  5  4</p>
<p>    Mauritius  4  0  1  3  3  8  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Zambia v Malawi, Lusaka, July 12</p>
<p>Mauritius v Mozambique, Curepipe, July 13)</p>
